<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Ms. Barton returns two months after her twelve-week review. The care manager&apos;s telephone PHQ-9 planned for about four weeks after that review was not completed: two calls in May went unanswered while she was at a week-long training course, and no further call was booked. She feels like herself again, with steady energy, and sleeps about seven hours. She has finished fifteen of sixteen CBT sessions and has joined the monthly peer support group. She works about 45 hours a week, walks most days, and sees friends weekly. She takes sertraline 100 mg every morning, has missed no doses, and has no side effects. She has had no suicidal thoughts. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Interval change</td><td>Feels like herself; steady energy</td></tr><tr><td>Missed contact</td><td>Telephone PHQ-9 planned in May not completed</td></tr><tr><td>Sleep</td><td>About seven hours</td></tr><tr><td>Psychotherapy</td><td>Fifteen of sixteen CBT sessions; monthly peer support group</td></tr><tr><td>Safety</td><td>No suicidal thoughts</td></tr><tr><td>PHQ-9</td><td>4</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

