    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Major depressive disorder, recurrent, in remission (F33.1)</content>. PHQ-9 4: remission, about five months after starting treatment. Because this is at least her second episode, the risk of recurrence is high. Suicide risk remains low. [S]<list><item>Continue sertraline 100 mg for at least twelve months after remission, then decide together about tapering or longer maintenance.</item><item>PHQ-9 every two to three months in continuation, with the care-manager registry flagging any missed call.</item><item>Finish the CBT course and keep the peer support group; agree early warning signs with her therapist.</item><item>Collaborative safety plan reviewed and unchanged; 988 Suicide &amp; Crisis Lifeline and the clinic number confirmed.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Occupational burnout (Z73.0)</content>. Recovered; keeping within the 45-hour limit. [S]<list><item>No field deployment before the spring; plan any return with her board and review here before and after.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Protocol monitoring: items the monitoring protocol calls for at this visit. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Measure</th><th>Interval</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Survey</td><td>PHQ-9</td><td>Baseline, then at least monthly during acute treatment; every 2 to 4 weeks in continuation</td><td>Completed today</td><td>4: remission</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Monthly PHQ-9 between the twelve-week review and today</td><td>At least monthly during acute treatment</td><td>Deferred</td><td>Not done, a deviation from the protocol: the care-manager telephone PHQ-9 planned for about four weeks after the twelve-week review was not completed after two unanswered calls, leaving nine weeks unmeasured. No harm resulted judging by today&apos;s review: she reached remission and had no suicidal thoughts. Corrective action: the registry now books a callback within a week after any unanswered call and alerts Dr. Whitcombe if a scheduled score is missing</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Suicide risk reassessment (C-SSRS Since Last Visit and PHQ-9 item 9)</td><td>Every visit during active treatment</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No suicidal thoughts, intent, plan, or behavior since the last visit; PHQ-9 item 9 scored 0. Protective factors stronger than at intake. Safety plan reviewed</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Adherence and adverse-effect review</td><td>Every visit during active treatment</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No missed doses; no side effects</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Psychotherapy, sleep, work hours, and social contact</td><td>Every visit during active treatment</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Fifteen of sixteen CBT sessions; sleep about seven hours; 45-hour week; monthly peer support group</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>Lithium, anticonvulsant, or antipsychotic monitoring (levels, metabolic tests, AIMS)</td><td>Only on those drugs</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Treated with an SSRI only</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Goal progress:</paragraph><list><item>Response (PHQ-9 down by at least 50 percent) by twelve weeks. Outcome by 2026-04-14: PHQ-9 7 at twelve weeks, down 61 percent from 18 [S]</item><item>Remission (PHQ-9 below 5) and continuation treatment for at least twelve months after remission. Outcome by 2026-06-16: Remission reached at five months (PHQ-9 4); continuation treatment under way [S]</item><item>Sleep at least six hours most nights. Outcome by 2026-04-14: About six and a half hours most nights by twelve weeks [S]</item><item>Phased return to work at no more than 45 hours a week, with no field deployment for at least six months. Outcome by 2026-06-16: Full duties at 45 hours a week from April; no deployment [S]</item><item>Time with friends or her faith community at least twice a week. Outcome by 2026-06-16: Weekly dinner with friends and weekly services [S]</item></list><paragraph>Guideline basis: VA/DoD Clinical Practice Guideline for the Management of Major Depressive Disorder (2022); VA/DoD Clinical Practice Guideline for Assessment and Management of Patients at Risk for Suicide (2024); CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, depression, bipolar, and mood disorders monograph (2026)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: PHQ-9 in two to three months; preventive visit in October. Next scheduled visit 2026-10-13: periodic adult preventive visit. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
